  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "commuter-intro",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -180,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "COMMUTER — 18 plates\n\nEvery commuter verifies a mobile number before booking. There is no anonymous path: hasVerifiedPhone() in the security rules refuses a ride creation without one, so the gate is the rule rather than the screen.\n\nRow 3 is the ride lifecycle. Note that in_transit has no cancel button — the passenger is physically in the vehicle, and the rules refuse that transition."
    },
    {
      "id": "commuter-pickup",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 830,
      "w": 390,
      "text": "Pickup defaults to where the commuter is standing: a GPS fix on load, reverse-geocoded into an address a driver can act on.\n\nA late fix never overwrites a point set by hand, and a denied permission falls back to the tap-to-set behaviour."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-intro",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -180,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "DRIVER — 11 plates\n\nEvery non-approved state hides the online switch AND the offer list, so a driver is never shown work they cannot legally take.\n\nOffers arrive one at a time, not as a broadcast: the greedy sweep pings the nearest untried driver alone for 15 seconds, so there is no race to tap first."
    },
    {
      "id": "admin-intro",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -180,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "ADMIN — 9 plates\n\nThe unverified-admin plate replaces the whole dashboard. The client resolves the admin role from the admins document alone, but the rules also require a confirmed address — without this screen the panel would load and every read beneath it would fail with a permission error explaining nothing.\n\nNo money appears anywhere: the fare engine was removed, and the app quotes no prices and stores none."
    }
  ],
  "launch": { "view": "canvas", "page": "page-1" }
}
